From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 07:05:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/imagination: Check the job's done fence on a timeout

pvr_queue_timedout_job() starts with
dma_fence_is_signaled(s_job->s_fence->parent). The scheduler arms the
timeout in drm_sched_job_begin() before run_job() and stores the parent
only after run_job() returns, so a job whose run_job() takes longer than
the timeout reaches the handler with a NULL parent, and
dma_fence_is_signaled() dereferences it.

Test job->done_fence instead. It is the fence run_job() returns as the
parent, and pvr_queue_prepare_job() initialises it before the job can be
on the pending list. Where the parent is set, both are the same fence.
Where it is not, the job is not done and the handler goes on to stop and
restart the queue, as for any other timeout.

Fixes: ee7cb7425314 ("drm/imagination: Don't timeout job if its fence has been signaled")
Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: with a test-only knob holding one run_job()
past a shortened scheduler timeout, a GL client's job timed out before
run_job() returned, the kernel stayed without an oops, and the client
and a later one rendered correctly.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_queue.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_queue.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_queue.c
index 24a8645aa913..ddbceda63f35 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_queue.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_queue.c
@@ -867,10 +867,17 @@ pvr_queue_timedout_job(struct drm_sched_job *s_job)
 	struct drm_gpu_scheduler *sched = s_job->sched;
 	struct pvr_queue *queue = container_of(sched, struct pvr_queue, scheduler);
 	struct pvr_device *pvr_dev = queue->ctx->pvr_dev;
-	struct pvr_job *job;
+	struct pvr_job *job = container_of(s_job, struct pvr_job, base);
 	u32 job_count = 0;
 
-	if (dma_fence_is_signaled(s_job->s_fence->parent))
+	/*
+	 * Not s_fence->parent: drm_sched arms this timeout before it calls
+	 * run_job(), and sets the parent only when run_job() returns, so a job
+	 * whose run_job() has not returned yet arrives here with a NULL parent.
+	 * The done fence is what run_job() returns as the parent, and
+	 * prepare_job() initialises it before the job reaches the pending list.
+	 */
+	if (dma_fence_is_signaled(job->done_fence))
 		return DRM_GPU_SCHED_STAT_NO_HANG;
 
 	dev_err(sched->dev, "Job timeout\n");
